The API client and wire models are derived from QBZ commit
455441014b38e27b1d0c4054e04e6a66aa2753db (MIT, copyright 2024 blitzkriegfc).
The MIT notices remain in crates/qobuz-api/LICENSE and
crates/qobuz-models/LICENSE.

The media implementation replaces the predecessor's parser, key interface,
lease management and transfer orchestration. Its protocol layouts were
studied from the predecessor; the retained MIT notice is in
crates/media-core/LICENSE. This is a source reimplementation, not a claim
of clean-room provenance.

Credential discovery and browser authentication follow Strawberry commit
aa2ba5109b1fbc9a1fe4de096644e5713b434f3b.
Strawberry copyright 2019-2026 Jonas Kvinge <jonas@jkvinge.net>.

The plugin is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later; see COPYING. The local
API, model and media crates retain their MIT license notices.

The library index uses rusqlite and bundled SQLite. The rusqlite,
libsqlite3-sys, iterator and hash-table notices are in LICENSE-INDEX.
SQLite itself is in the public domain.

Article text uses html-escape and utf8-width. Their MIT notices are included
in LICENSE-INDEX.

QBZ catalog and plugin contracts derive from the Chilpa Qobuz source plugin
(GPL-3.0-or-later). The retired browser/OAuth source files are not used by QBZ.

Firefox early injection and action bridge derive from matthewprince/zbq
v0.1.1, commit 2d73f2c00983a3adb696220b09047b6468bd0072, MIT.
The upstream notice is retained in browser/vendor/LICENSE.
The companion capture, progressive PCM relay and setup wizard are QBZ code.

The companion includes Python (PSF license), aiohttp (Apache-2.0/MIT),
websockets (BSD-3-Clause), and PySide6/Qt (LGPL-3.0/GPL alternatives).
Their distributed notices remain with the bundled libraries. FFmpeg and
Firefox are selected external installations and are not bundled.

The plugin icon is the original QBZ monochrome tray icon (tray-dark-64.png, 64 px), supplied from
the QBZ project for this integration.
